B.FX=new A.V(5,"The square you must not fill",B.O,"You never choose a square, only a column \u2014 and your piece makes the square above it available to them. Sometimes one column is poisoned and every other move is fine.",B.ax,B.I0,null,null,B.HA,"Dropping into column 6 puts your piece directly under the square the amber sunbursts need, and they take it on the next turn. Nothing else on the board is urgent, so simply play elsewhere. Before any move, ask what your piece opens up, not only what it builds.",!0,B.i,null,null)
